d2d1: Do not stream the figures of a path geometry whose Close failed.

When ID2D1GeometrySink::Close fails (triangulation gives up: "Triangle not found", or a segment that does not
converge, 0061), the path's figures are freed but figure_count kept its value. A geometry group built from such a
path (CreateGeometryGroup streams every source geometry into its own path) then walked figure_count entries of a
NULL array: an access violation in d2d_path_geometry_stream, inside a window message. Wine's user callback
handler swallowed it ("ignoring exception c0000005") and unwound out of the window procedure, so After Effects was
left half way through building its Render Queue panel: the panel never painted and AE stopped its idle work
(BridgeTalk scripts timed out) while the main thread waited in GetMessage (2026-10-23, +msg,+seh traces). Reset
figure_count with the figures, and stream nothing for a path that is not closed. The Render Queue panel now
paints, and Composition > Add to Render Queue, Output To and Render work by hand.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c
@@ -3503,6 +3503,7 @@
     free(geometry->u.path.figures);
     geometry->u.path.figures = NULL;
     geometry->u.path.figures_size = 0;
+    geometry->u.path.figure_count = 0;
 }
 
 static BOOL d2d_geometry_get_bezier_segment_idx(struct d2d_geometry *geometry, struct d2d_segment_idx *idx, BOOL next)
@@ -4619,6 +4620,11 @@
 {
     unsigned int flags = 0;
 
+    /* A path whose Close failed has no figures left; a geometry group or a transformed
+     * geometry built from it streams nothing. */
+    if (geometry->u.path.state != D2D_GEOMETRY_STATE_CLOSED)
+        return;
+
     if (transform)
         return d2d_path_geometry_transformed_stream(geometry, transform, sink);
 
